# {{ obcell_name }} Obcell runbook

Private 4G/5G network (Open5GS + OCUDU gNB on a {{ sdr.name }}, band {{ cell_label }}) with remote-production
tools (Open Live, Open Intercom) and monitoring, on one {{ obcell_hardware_desc | default(ansible_processor_vcpus ~ '-CPU machine') }}. Day-to-day work goes through
the `obcell` command (`obcell help`; the old name `kit` still works).

> **{{ cell_label }} ({{ cell_freq_label ~ ' MHz' }}) is licensed spectrum.** Only put the cell on air with a test permit, or cabled/shielded.
> The gNB **does not start at boot**: it only goes on air when someone presses ON AIR or runs `obcell onair`.
> (`obcell boot-onair on` would change that; `obcell status` always shows the current setting.)

## Addresses

Start at the portal: {{ ('**https://' ~ obcell_tailnet_name ~ '** (tailnet) or ') if obcell_tailnet_name else '' }}**https://{{ obcell_mdns_name }}** (LAN). Both names use the same ports.
One Authelia login covers everything except Intercom guests.

| Service | Tailnet (`{{ obcell_tailnet_name }}`) | LAN (`{{ obcell_mdns_name }}`, or `{{ obcell_lan_ip }}` for most) |
|---|---|---|
| Homepage portal + on-air buttons | `/` or `:5443` | `/` or `:5443` |
| Open Live Studio | `:7443` | `:7443` (`{{ obcell_mdns_name }}` only) |
| Open Intercom (guests: no login) | `:8443` | `:8443` |
| Grafana (dashboards, alert list) | `:3443` | `:3443` |
| ntopng | `:4443` | `:4443` |
| OpenWebRX+ (RTL-SDR) | `:6443` | `:6443` |
| Open5GS WebUI (subscribers; then its own admin password) | `:{{ open5gs_webui_https_port }}` | `:{{ open5gs_webui_https_port }}` |

- **Tailnet:** uses real Let's Encrypt certificates, fetched by Caddy from tailscaled.
- **LAN:** uses Caddy's internal CA. Devices need `~/openlive/openlive-root-ca.crt` installed.
- **Old LAN address:** `https://{{ obcell_mdns_name }}` used to be Open Live. Bookmarks now land on Homepage; Open Live is on `:7443`. `https://{{ obcell_lan_ip }}` redirects to the LAN portal.
- **Intercom audio:** goes to UDP {{ obcell_lan_ip }}:10000. Tailnet devices reach it through the approved subnet route {{ obcell_lan_ip }}/32.

